Clauses & Conditions:
The Visual & Text Transparency Clause:
Any redistribution of this Software—whether distributed as visual block projects, raw C++ source code, or compiled native binaries—must preserve the ability for end-users to inspect the underlying code generation. The "Code Shower" or equivalent text-inspection mechanism must remain accessible so users can view how visual logic translates into native code.

Attribution & Origin:
The original creator, Leovanni, must be prominently credited as the primary architect of the core platform structure in all substantial distributions, documentation, and derivative works.

Extension Compatibility:
Extensions built using the JSON/JS DSL format for this platform may be distributed under licenses chosen by their respective authors, provided they do not restrict the core execution engine's ability to transpile and compile them into native binaries.

